7. Term: This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and continue until the first annual anniversary of the Effective Date, at which time this Agreement shall automatically renew for successive one (1) year terms, unless terminated as provided below, which termination can occur any time in accordance with Paragraph 8 of this Agreement.

8. Termination: Either Party may terminate this Agreement, with or without cause, by furnishing the other Party written notice of such termination. If this Agreement is terminated, all obligations of either Party shall cease on the date of such termination.

NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT

1. The Contractor acknowledges that, while providing services to The Linguals, they may receive access to confidential and proprietary information belonging to the Company and its clients. This Agreement is intended to protect such information and ensure professional, secure, and ethical handling of all assignments.

2. For the purpose of this Agreement, Confidential Information includes, but is not limited to, client details, project information, source files, translation materials, documents, audio and video files, software, applications, websites, databases, terminology, glossaries, style guides, pricing information, business strategies, contracts, communications, technical information, AI datasets, personal data, and any other information that is not publicly available.

3. The Contractor agrees to keep all Confidential Information strictly private and shall use such information only for completing assigned work for The Linguals. The Contractor shall not disclose, share, reproduce, publish, sell, distribute, or provide any Company or client information to any third party, and the Contractor shall not claim ownership, reuse, publish, or distribute such materials without written permission.

4. The Contractor shall not upload, submit, or process any confidential Company or client material through public artificial intelligence tools, machine translation systems, online platforms, or third-party software unless such use has been specifically proved by The Linguals or the relevant client.

5. The Contractor agrees not to directly contact, solicit, or accept work from any client introduced through The Linguals without prior written approval from the Company. The Contractor also agrees not to misuse confidential relationships, business information, or internal contacts obtained through the Company for personal or competitive purposes.

6. The Contractor shall maintain appropriate security measures while working remotely, including protecting files, devices, passwords, and communication channels. Any accidental disclosure, security breach, or unauthorized access involving Company or client information must immediately be reported to The Linguals.

7. Upon completion of assignments or upon request by the Company, the Contractor shall return or permanently delete all confidential files and materials belonging to The Linguals or its clients.

8. The Contractor acknowledges that unauthorized disclosure or misuse of confidential information may cause serious harm to The Linguals and its clients. The Company reserves the right to seek appropriate legal remedies, including damages and injunctive relief, in case of breach of this Agreement.

9. This Agreement does not create an employment relationship, partnership, or agency relationship between the Parties. The Contractor shall act as an independent contractor unless otherwise agreed in writing.

